# persona-ownership — Machine-Readable Persona & Canonical Host Ownership Registry (SSoT)
File: openOODA/persona-ownership.oot

This registry is the normative Single Source of Truth (SSoT) for multi-call persona dispatch
and repository consolidation across `@openOODA-core` (L0) through `@openOODA-agents` (L7) per
`rfcs/0012-unix-less-is-more-consolidation.oot` and `rules.oot` §1.25.

## 1. Constitutional Ownership Invariants
1. **Single Owner Per Token**: Every persona token and absorbed repository name maps to
   EXACTLY ONE canonical host binary. Dual-host embeddings and mutual absorption cycles are
   constitutional violations (`E_PERSONA_DUP`).
2. **Flat Hierarchy (No Nested Personas)**: A canonical host binary MUST NOT itself be a
   persona of another host binary. Former intermediate hosts (`oocockpit`, `oolock`,
   `ooreviewer`) are demoted to direct personas of their canonical parent host.
3. **Zero Catalog Double-Ships**: No persona token owned by a consolidated host may be
   published as a standalone package entry in `openOODA/catalog/index`.
4. **Zero Link Aliases (`rules.oot` §1.25)**: Persona tokens are selected via `--persona <name>`,
   `--mode <name>`, or leading subcommand token (`<host> <persona> [args...]`), NEVER via
   filesystem symlinks or hardlinks.

## 2. Canonical Host & Persona Ownership Table (`ORG | CANONICAL_HOST | RENAME_FROM | ABSORBED_REPOS_AND_PERSONA_TOKENS`)

